<title>UK: British govt loses key committee vote on EMU.</title>
<headline>British govt loses key committee vote on EMU.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The British government on Wednesday lost a key vote in a committee scrutinising aspects of economic and monetary union, sparking demands for a full-scale debate on the European Union on the floor of the House of Commons.</p>
<p>The government has been furiously striving to avoid such a debate for fear that it would expose divisions in the ruling Conservative party.</p>
</text>
